# Z8001 segmented-mode clock cycles, from the Z8000 CPU Technical Manual
# (Mar 1981) section 6.7.  One line per instruction and addressing mode:
#   MNEMONIC MODE SS [SL]
# SS is the short-offset (or only) figure, SL the long-offset one for DA and
# X.  Modes: R IM IR DA X BA BX RA, and "-" for instructions with no operand
# mode.  A mnemonic ending in "<" is the store form of a load (memory
# destination).  Byte forms (LDB, ADDB, ...) use the word line unless they
# have their own.  Shifts, multiply, divide, LDM and conditional returns are
# priced in fpcycles.py.
ADC   R  5
SBC   R  5
ADD   R  4
ADD   IM 7
ADD   IR 7
ADD   DA 10 12
ADD   X  10 13
ADDL  R  8
ADDL  IM 14
ADDL  IR 14
ADDL  DA 16 18
ADDL  X  16 19
SUB   R  4
SUB   IM 7
SUB   IR 7
SUB   DA 10 12
SUB   X  10 13
SUBL  R  8
SUBL  IM 14
SUBL  IR 14
SUBL  DA 16 18
SUBL  X  16 19
AND   R  4
AND   IM 7
AND   IR 7
AND   DA 10 12
AND   X  10 13
OR    R  4
OR    IM 7
OR    IR 7
OR    DA 10 12
OR    X  10 13
XOR   R  4
XOR   IM 7
XOR   IR 7
XOR   DA 10 12
XOR   X  10 13
CP    R  4
CP    IM 7
CP    IR 7
CP    DA 10 12
CP    X  10 13
CPL   R  8
CPL   IM 14
CPL   IR 14
CPL   DA 16 18
CPL   X  16 19
BIT   R  4
BIT   IR 8
BIT   DA 11 13
BIT   X  11 14
SET   R  4
RES   R  4
CLR   R  7
CLR   IR 8
CLR   DA 12 14
CLR   X  12 15
COM   R  7
NEG   R  7
TEST  R  7
TEST  IR 8
TEST  DA 12 14
TEST  X  12 15
TESTL R  13
TESTL IR 13
TESTL DA 17 19
TESTL X  17 20
INC   R  4
INC   IR 11
INC   DA 14 16
INC   X  14 17
DEC   R  4
DEC   IR 11
DEC   DA 14 16
DEC   X  14 17
EX    R  6
EXTS  R  11
EXTSB R  11
EXTSL R  11
LDK   R  5
LD    R  3
LD    IM 7
LD    IR 7
LD    DA 10 12
LD    X  10 13
LD    BA 14
LD    BX 14
LD<   IR 8
LD<   DA 12 14
LD<   X  12 15
LD<   BA 14
LD<   BX 14
LDB   IM 5
LDL   R  5
LDL   IM 11
LDL   IR 11
LDL   DA 13 15
LDL   X  13 16
LDL   BA 17
LDL   BX 17
LDL<  IR 11
LDL<  DA 15 17
LDL<  X  15 18
LDL<  BA 17
LDL<  BX 17
LDA   DA 13 15
LDA   X  13 16
LDA   BA 15
LDA   BX 15
LDR   RA 14
LDRL  RA 17
LDR<  RA 14
LDRL< RA 17
LDAR  RA 15
PUSH  R  9
PUSH  IM 12
PUSH  IR 13
PUSH  DA 14 17
PUSH  X  14 17
PUSHL R  12
PUSHL IR 20
PUSHL DA 21 24
PUSHL X  21 24
POP   R  8
POP   IR 12
POP   DA 16 18
POP   X  16 19
POPL  R  12
POPL  IR 19
POPL  DA 23 25
POPL  X  23 26
JR    RA 6
DJNZ  RA 11
DBJNZ RA 11
CALR  RA 15
CALL  IR 15
CALL  DA 18 20
CALL  X  18 21
JP    DA 8 10
JP    X  11 11
SC    IM 39
RLC   R  6
RRC   R  6
RL    R  6
RR    R  6
RLDB  R  9
RRDB  R  9
SETFLG - 7
RESFLG - 7
NOP   -  7
